Using the following identities:
$$
{}^{s_{2}}P_1(rts)={}^{s_{1}}P_2(srt),
$$$$
(\tau_2^{2}){}^{s_{2}}Q_2(rts)Q_2(rst)=(1-P_{2}(rst))(q+P_{2}(rst)),
$$
$$
(\tau_1^{2}){}^{s_{1}}Q_1(srt)Q_1(rst)=(1-P_{1}(rst))(q+P_{1}(rst)),
$$
we need to check that
\begin{align*}
P_2(rst)^{2}&(P_1(rst)-{}^{s_{2}}P_1(rts))+(1-q)P_2(rst){}^{s_{2}}P_1(rts)\\&=P_1(rst)^{2}(P_2(rst)-{}^{s_{1}}P_2(srt))+(1-q)P_1(rst){}^{s_{1}}P_2(srt).
\end{align*}
By an explicit expansion, it is easy to see that the left hand side and right hand side are both equal to
\begin{align*}
(1-q)^{3}\frac{st^{2}(x_2+1)(x_{3}+1)^{2}}{(t(x_{3}+1)-s(x_{2}+1))(t(x_{3}+1)-r(x_{1}+1))(s(x_{2}+1)-r(x_{1}+1))}.
\end{align*}

